 one patch-agent session complete more than one reviewed patch without a later hash replacing earlier
 reviewed work in the linearizer prompt.
 
+When automatic or explicit review completes with resolved findings for a user patch agent, the
+controller asks that patch agent's chat whether the feature is done. A `yes` or `y` answer records
+the feature as done without resuming the backend agent. A `no` or `n` answer keeps the feature open.
+Any other follow-up reopens a previously closed feature and resumes the selected patch agent with
+the follow-up text.
+
 The command transcript is also the conversation history for the persistent `command-agent`. That
 system agent interprets chat sent to the Work Leaf command surface. It recognizes literal command
 lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching
@@ -300,9 +306,11 @@ When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the
 path.
 
 The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading
-state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
+state for that session and the session has not been marked done through the reviewed-feature
+confirmation prompt. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
-again.
+again, or until the feature is marked done. Follow-up text that reopens the feature can make the
+session eligible for the ready marker again.
 
